<article class="env-lemma" id="0G3C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G3C">Lemma <span data-tag="0G3C">13.42.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a triangulated category. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  A_ n \to B_ n \to C_ n \to A_ n[1]  \]
</div>
  <p> be an inverse system of distinguished triangles. If the system $C_ n$ is pro-zero (essentially constant with value $0$), then the maps $A_ n \to B_ n$ determine a pro-isomorphism between the pro-object $(A_ n)$ and the pro-object $(B_ n)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For any object $X$ of $\mathcal{D}$ consider the exact sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (C_ n, X) \to \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (B_ n, X) \to \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (A_ n, X) \to \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (C_ n[-1], X) \to  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Exactness follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0149" data-tag="0149">13.4.2</a> combined with Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00DB" data-tag="00DB">10.8.8</a>. By assumption the first and last term are zero. Hence the map $\mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (B_ n, X) \to \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (A_ n, X)$ is an isomorphism for all $X$. The lemma follows from this and Categories, Remark <a href="/tag/0G2X" data-tag="0G2X">4.22.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>